# `js/` port conventions

## Modules and delivery

- Use **ES modules** (`import` / `export`). No bundler; code must run in **Node 22+** and modern browsers as-is.
- Do not modify **frozen** files: `js/isaac64.js`, `js/terminal.js`, `js/storage.js` (see always-on contest rule).

## RNG and C parity

- The C recorder is built with **clang**; argument evaluation is effectively **left-to-right**. When one expression makes multiple RNG calls (e.g. `d(rn2(a), rn2(b))`), match that order in JS — see [README.md](README.md) gcc vs clang note.
- Route gameplay RNG through the wrappers in [js/rng.js](js/rng.js) so logging and semantics stay aligned with the harness.

## Skeleton vs real port

- [js/fastforward.js](js/fastforward.js) is **temporary** replay scaffolding. **Remove** replay rows when real `js/` logic matches C RNG at that call site — do **not** extend fastforward to “fix” score without porting C ([`port-from-c-not-score.mdc`](port-from-c-not-score.mdc)).
- [js/monmove.js](js/monmove.js) `_HARNESS` (and similar) are the same: peel only when per-path draws match `monmove.c`, not when a session index “needs” a value.

## API surface

- Contest entry: `runSegment` and `NethackGame` in [js/jsmain.js](js/jsmain.js). Full contract: [docs/API.md](docs/API.md).
